00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.007
Unsurprisingly, "The White Lotus" is&nbsp;
just as exciting behind-the-scenes.

00:00:10.007 --> 00:00:15.480
"The White Lotus" fans were excited when "Parks&nbsp;
and Recreation" star Aubrey Plaza decided to join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.460
the show for its second season. Plaza stars as&nbsp;
Harper, a lawyer vacationing in Sicily with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.440
husband Ethan, his college friend Cameron, and&nbsp;
Cameron's wife Daphne. After arriving at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.120
resort, tensions start to arise as Harper quickly&nbsp;
realizes that she dislikes her husband's friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.500
Throughout the season, Harper's judgmental&nbsp;
tendencies ruffle more than a few feathers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.480
But what fans may not know is that Plaza&nbsp;
hilariously caused some chaos off-screen, too.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.700
While filming "The White Lotus," Plaza pulled some&nbsp;
pretty extravagant pranks on her co-stars, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.800
she referred to as a "Charlie Kaufman experiment"&nbsp;
during an interview with GQ. At one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:55.080
she collected all the diffusers scattered around&nbsp;
the hotel and arranged them into a creepy pattern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.300
in the dressing room of co-star Adam DiMarco, who&nbsp;
played Albie. Of Plaza's antics, DiMarco told GQ,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.100
The "Child's Play" star even went so far as to&nbsp;
mess up her own dressing room to deflect blame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.700
convincing the other actors that she&nbsp;
had nothing to do with the pranks.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.320
The setting of "The White Lotus" Season 1&nbsp;
is utterly breathtaking. Shot on location&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.220
at the Four Seasons Resort in Maui,&nbsp;
episodes feature pristine blue water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.140
fluffy white beaches, and picturesque palm trees.&nbsp;
While the setting was undeniably beautiful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.680
the location could actually get pretty&nbsp;
distracting at times. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.180
Natasha Rothwell, who plays Belinda in the&nbsp;
show's first season, revealed that some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.080
Maui's features often made it difficult to&nbsp;
concentrate when the cameras were rolling.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.460
The actor recounted a particular scene she&nbsp;
filmed on a boat alongside Jennifer Coolidge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.120
who plays an extremely wealthy&nbsp;
guest named Tanya. During the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.169
Tanya scatters her mother's&nbsp;
ashes off the side of the boat.

00:01:54.169 --> 00:01:59.689
"I brought my mother's ashes with me, you&nbsp;
know, so I could spread them in the ocean."

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:04.680
However, while filming, Rothwell found herself&nbsp;
becoming distracted by the fascinating sea life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.060
surrounding them, including some whales.&nbsp;
As Rothwell told The Hollywood Reporter,

